sketchBlocks.bodyMarkdown:
Use `for...of` when you need to perform the same kind of work for every item in an array.

```js
const eventNames = ["Welcome Fair", "Jazz Night", "Poetry Reading"];

for (const name of eventNames) {
  console.log(name);
}
```

Step by step:

1. `eventNames` contains three strings.
2. `for (const name of eventNames)` starts one pass for each array item.
3. During each pass, `name` refers to the current string.
4. `console.log(name)` runs three times, once per item.

The loop does not require you to manage numeric indexes when you only need each value directly.

